    <bpmn:process id="W_W1250" name="W1250. Store Foot Traffic Analytics, Conversion Rate Monitoring &amp; Sales Floor Productivity Insights" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Scheduled — weekly foot traffic analytics refresh; monthly productivity deep-dive; ad-hoc triggered by store conversion rate decline or regional benchmarking request
Frequency: Weekly analytics refresh; monthly deep-dive per store; quarterly regional benchmarking
Volume: 200 stores × weekly analytics; monthly deep-dive for bottom-quartile stores (50 stores); quarterly benchmarking for all stores by region
Owner: BI Analyst (Retail Analytics)
Participants: Store Manager, Regional Manager, VP Store Operations, Category Manager, Facilities Manager
Source: workflow W1250 — Store Foot Traffic Analytics, Conversion Rate Monitoring &amp; Sales Floor Productivity Insights</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1250_LaneSet2">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1250_Lane1" name="BI Analyst">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1250_Task4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1250_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1250_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1250_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1250_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1250_Start3</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1250_End9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1250_Start3" name="Scheduled — weekly foot traffic analytics refresh; monthly productivity deep-dive; ad-hoc…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1250_Flow12</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1250_Task4" name="Weekly foot traffic data collection &amp; processing">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Weekly foot traffic data collection &amp; processing: BI Analyst extracts and processes foot traffic data from store-level people counters (door-mounted infrared or video-based counters): (a) aggregate daily entry counts by store; (b) calculate conversion rate: POS transactions ÷ foot traffic entries; (c) calculate ATV (average transaction value) and items per basket; (d) compute sales per sqm using store selling area from location master; (e) flag stores where conversion rate dropped &gt; 10% week-over-week
Responsible (R): BI Analyst
Accountable (A): BI Manager
Duration: 3 hours/week</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1250_Flow12</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1250_Flow12</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1250_Task5" name="Conversion rate variance analysis">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Conversion rate variance analysis: For flagged stores, investigate conversion rate decline: (a) cross-reference with promotional calendar — was the store running an event that drove traffic without conversion? (b) check staffing levels during peak traffic hours — understaffing reduces conversion; (c) review out-of-stock rate for top-selling SKUs — stock-outs reduce conversion; (d) check weather data — heavy rain in provincial locations depresses walk-in traffic; (e) compile findings for Regional Manager review
Responsible (R): BI Analyst
Accountable (A): Regional Manager
Duration: 2 hours/week</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1250_Flow13</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1250_Flow13</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1250_Task6" name="Monthly sales floor productivity deep-dive">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Monthly sales floor productivity deep-dive: For bottom-quartile stores (50 stores by conversion rate), conduct detailed analysis: (a) zone-level traffic heat map (if zone-level sensors available) showing dwell time in lumber yard, tool wall, tile gallery, appliance section, checkout; (b) category-level conversion — which departments have high traffic but low sales; (c) staffing-to-traffic ratio — sales associates per 100 visitors by hour; (d) queue wait time correlation — does checkout queue length correlate with abandoned purchases; (e) generate store-specific productivity improvement recommendations
Responsible (R): BI Analyst / Regional Manager
Accountable (A): VP Store Operations
Duration: 4 hours/month</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1250_Flow14</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1250_Flow14</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1250_Task7" name="Quarterly regional benchmarking report">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Quarterly regional benchmarking report: BI Analyst produces quarterly benchmarking report comparing all 200 stores across: (a) foot traffic growth rate (YoY, QoQ); (b) conversion rate ranking by region (Mindanao, Visayas, Luzon, NCR); (c) ATV trends by store maturity (new stores &lt; 1 year vs. mature stores &gt; 3 years); (d) sales per sqm vs. foot traffic per sqm — identifying over/under-performing space; (e) present to VP Store Operations and CMO for strategic decisions on marketing spend allocation, store hours optimization, and layout renovation priorities
Responsible (R): BI Analyst / BI Manager
Accountable (A): VP Store Operations
Duration: 8 hours/quarter</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1250_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1250_Flow15</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1250_Task8" name="Action plan tracking">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Action plan tracking: Track implementation and impact of productivity improvement actions: (a) for each recommended action (staffing adjustment, layout change, category refresh), measure before/after conversion rate and ATV; (b) report ROI of layout changes and capital improvements; (c) feed results into annual store capital budget process
Responsible (R): BI Analyst
Accountable (A): Regional Manager
Duration: 2 hours/month</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1250_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1250_End9" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1250_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1250_Annotation10">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-325 (ensure controlled execution — BI Platform &amp; Reporting (PA-28.1).) | - operational: BI Analyst (Retail Analytics) review and approval gate
Owner: BI Analyst (Retail Analytics)</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W1250_Assoc11" sourceRef="W1250_Annotation10" targetRef="W1250_Start3" associationDirection="None" />
