    <bpmn:process id="W_W1451" name="W1451. Merchandise Category Performance Analytics, Gross Margin Optimization &amp; Assortment Rationalization Insights" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Monthly category performance reporting cycle; or quarterly assortment review; or ad-hoc request from VP Merchandising or Category Manager
Frequency: Monthly reporting; quarterly deep-dive analysis; annual assortment rationalization review
Volume: 12 product categories; 35,000 active SKUs; 200 stores; ~PHP 62.3B annual revenue across all categories
Owner: BI Analytics Manager
Participants: BI Analytics Manager, Data Analyst, VP Merchandising, Category Managers, Pricing Analyst, Finance Controller, VP Store Operations
Source: workflow W1451 — Merchandise Category Performance Analytics, Gross Margin Optimization &amp; Assortment Rationalization Insights</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1451_LaneSet4">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1451_Lane1" name="Data Analyst">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1451_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1451_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1451_Start5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1451_Lane2" name="BI Analytics Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1451_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1451_Lane3" name="Category Managers">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1451_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1451_End10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1451_Start5" name="Monthly category performance reporting cycle; or quarterly assortment review; or ad-hoc…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1451_Flow13</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1451_Task6" name="Monthly category performance dashboard">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Monthly category performance dashboard: Data Analyst produces monthly category scorecard: (a) revenue by category: (i) actual vs. plan vs. prior year, (ii) revenue share (% of total), (iii) same-store sales growth, (b) gross margin by category: (i) gross margin %, (ii) gross margin PHP, (iii) margin variance drivers (mix, pricing, cost changes), (c) inventory productivity: (i) GMROI (gross margin ÷ average inventory cost), (ii) inventory turns by category, (iii) weeks of supply, (d) space productivity: (i) sales per sqm by department, (ii) gross margin per sqm — identifies departments where space reallocation would improve store profitability
Responsible (R): Data Analyst
Accountable (A): BI Analytics Manager
Duration: 8 hours/month</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1451_Flow13</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1451_Flow13</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1451_Task7" name="SKU-level margin analysis">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: SKU-level margin analysis (quarterly): Data Analyst conducts deep-dive margin analysis: (a) for each category, rank all SKUs by gross margin contribution (top 20% of SKUs typically drive 80% of margin), (b) identify &quot;margin leakers&quot;: high-velocity SKUs with below-target margin — evaluate: (i) is the cost increasing? (vendor price increase, landed cost change per W85), (ii) is pricing competitive? (competitor pricing data), (iii) recommended action: negotiate vendor cost reduction, increase SRP, or discontinue, (c) identify &quot;margin gems&quot;: low-velocity SKUs with high margin — evaluate: (i) can velocity be increased through better placement/promotion?, (ii) are these niche products worth keeping in assortment?, (d) identify &quot;dead weight&quot;: low-velocity, low-margin SKUs — candidates for discontinuation per W1
Responsible (R): Data Analyst / Category Manager
Accountable (A): VP Merchandising
Duration: 16 hours/quarter</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1451_Flow14</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1451_Flow14</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1451_Task8" name="Assortment rationalization recommendation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Assortment rationalization recommendation (annual): BI Analytics Manager produces annual assortment rationalization report: (a) SKU lifecycle analysis: (i) new SKU performance vs. forecast (first 90 days), (ii) active SKU performance (sales velocity, margin, GMROI), (iii) declining SKU trend (12-month sales trend — is the SKU dying?), (iv) dead SKU identification (zero sales in 90 days), (b) market gap analysis: (i) competitor assortment comparison — categories where BuildRight has fewer SKUs than competitors, (ii) customer search queries on buildright.com.ph with zero results — products customers want but BuildRight doesn&#x27;t carry, (c) recommendation: (i) SKUs to discontinue (target: 2,000–3,000/year), (ii) SKUs to add (target: 2,000–4,000/year for net 5–8% SKU growth), (iii) space reallocation recommendations by department, (d) present to VP Merchandising and Category Managers for action planning
Responsible (R): BI Analytics Manager
Accountable (A): VP Merchandising
Duration: 40 hours/year</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1451_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1451_Flow15</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1451_Task9" name="Category action plan tracking">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Category action plan tracking: VP Merchandising and Category Managers develop action plans based on analytics insights: (a) cost reduction actions: vendor negotiation for high-cost SKUs (target: reduce COGS by 1–2% on top 500 SKUs), (b) pricing actions: SRP adjustments for margin leakers (per W13 pricing governance), (c) assortment actions: discontinuation list, new SKU introduction list, (d) BI Analytics Manager tracks action plan execution and measures impact on subsequent months&#x27; category scorecards
Responsible (R): Category Managers / BI Manager
Accountable (A): VP Merchandising
Duration: Ongoing</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1451_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1451_End10" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1451_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1451_Annotation11">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-325 (ensure controlled execution — BI Platform &amp; Reporting (PA-28.1).) | - operational: standard operating procedures; system-enforced validation rules
Owner: BI Analytics Manager</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
