    <bpmn:process id="W_W1452" name="W1452. Customer Segmentation &amp; Lifetime Value Analytics: Trade Professional vs. Retail vs. Corporate Account Profiling" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Quarterly customer analytics cycle; or annual marketing strategy planning; or loyalty program review per W104
Frequency: Quarterly segmentation refresh; annual deep-dive with lifetime value modeling; monthly monitoring dashboards
Volume: ~600,000 loyalty members (B2C); ~5,200 trade accounts (B2B); ~200 corporate accounts (B2B); ~42,900 ecommerce customers/month
Owner: BI Analytics Manager
Participants: BI Analytics Manager, Data Scientist, VP Marketing, CMO, Trade Account Manager, CRM Manager, VP Merchandising
Source: workflow W1452 — Customer Segmentation &amp; Lifetime Value Analytics: Trade Professional vs. Retail vs. Corporate Account Profiling</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1452_LaneSet4">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1452_Lane1" name="Data Scientist">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1452_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1452_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1452_Start5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1452_Lane2" name="BI Analytics Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1452_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1452_Lane3" name="Data Analyst">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1452_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1452_End10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1452_Start5" name="Quarterly customer analytics cycle; or annual marketing strategy planning; or loyalty…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1452_Flow13</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1452_Task6" name="Quarterly segmentation refresh">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Quarterly segmentation refresh: Data Scientist refreshes customer segmentation model: (a) RFM analysis (Recency, Frequency, Monetary) for all 605,200+ customers: (i) Recency: days since last purchase, (ii) Frequency: number of transactions in trailing 12 months, (iii) Monetary: total spend in trailing 12 months, (b) segment classification: (i) Retail Champions: top 10% by spend (loyalty members who shop frequently and spend heavily), (ii) Retail Regulars: middle 50% (steady but moderate shoppers), (iii) Retail At-Risk: previously active but declining (trigger win-back per loyalty program), (iv) Trade Active: trade accounts with purchases in last 90 days, (v) Trade Dormant: trade accounts with no purchases in 90+ days (trigger re-engagement), (vi) Corporate Active: corporate accounts with active projects, (vii) Corporate Pipeline: corporate accounts with upcoming project bids, (c) update customer master records with segment tags for targeted marketing per W83 and W1443
Responsible (R): Data Scientist
Accountable (A): BI Analytics Manager
Duration: 16 hours/quarter</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1452_Flow13</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1452_Flow13</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1452_Task7" name="Lifetime value modeling">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Lifetime value modeling (annual): Data Scientist builds/updates customer lifetime value (CLV) model: (a) historical CLV by segment: (i) average annual spend × average customer tenure × gross margin %, (ii) Trade professionals: avg PHP 300K/year × 5-year avg tenure × 25% margin = PHP 375K lifetime value, (iii) Retail Champions: avg PHP 50K/year × 3-year avg tenure × 32% margin = PHP 48K lifetime value, (iv) Corporate accounts: avg PHP 5M/year × 3-year avg tenure × 20% margin = PHP 3M lifetime value, (b) predictive CLV: machine learning model predicts future value based on purchasing patterns, demographics, and engagement signals, (c) customer acquisition cost (CAC) by segment: marketing spend ÷ new customers acquired, (d) CLV:CAC ratio by segment — guides marketing budget allocation (target: CLV:CAC &gt; 3:1)
Responsible (R): Data Scientist
Accountable (A): CMO
Duration: 40 hours/year</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1452_Flow14</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1452_Flow14</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1452_Task8" name="Segment-specific insight generation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Segment-specific insight generation: BI Analytics Manager produces segment-specific insights for stakeholders: (a) for VP Marketing: (i) which segment should receive increased marketing investment (highest CLV:CAC ratio), (ii) win-back campaign targets (At-Risk and Dormant segments), (iii) cross-sell/upsell opportunities (retail customers buying project materials who could be trade account candidates), (b) for VP Merchandising: (i) basket analysis by segment (what trade pros buy vs. retail customers — different category affinities), (ii) private label penetration by segment, (c) for VP Store Operations: (i) trade pro visit frequency and preferred store hours (inform staffing), (ii) BOPIS adoption by segment, (d) for CFO: (i) credit risk by segment (corporate account aging), (ii) margin by segment
Responsible (R): BI Analytics Manager
Accountable (A): CMO / VP Merchandising
Duration: 16 hours/quarter</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1452_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1452_Flow15</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1452_Task9" name="Monthly segment monitoring dashboard">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Monthly segment monitoring dashboard: Data Analyst maintains real-time segment dashboard: (a) active customer count by segment, (b) monthly spend by segment vs. plan, (c) new customer acquisition by segment, (d) churn rate by segment (customers who haven&#x27;t purchased in 90 days), (e) segment migration (customers moving between segments — e.g., Retail Regular → Trade Account upgrade), (f) alert on significant segment shifts: (i) trade account churn &gt; 5% in a month, (ii) retail active customer decline &gt; 2% month-over-month
Responsible (R): Data Analyst
Accountable (A): BI Analytics Manager
Duration: 8 hours/month</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1452_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1452_End10" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1452_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1452_Annotation11">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-325 (ensure controlled execution — BI Platform &amp; Reporting (PA-28.1).) | - operational: standard operating procedures; system-enforced validation rules
Owner: BI Analytics Manager</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W1452_Assoc12" sourceRef="W1452_Annotation11" targetRef="W1452_Start5" associationDirection="None" />
