    <bpmn:process id="W_W1567" name="W1567. Store Manager Self-Service Analytics Dashboard, Daily KPI Monitoring &amp; Actionable Insight Delivery" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Daily — automated dashboard refresh at 6:00 AM (pre-store opening); real-time during store operating hours for select KPIs
Frequency: Daily dashboard refresh; weekly trend summary auto-emailed to Store Manager; monthly deep-dive analytics available on demand
Volume: 200 stores × 1 Store Manager dashboard = 200 daily dashboard views; ~180–200 Store Managers viewing daily during morning walkthrough (the &gt;90% adoption target)
Owner: BI Analytics Manager
Participants: BI Analytics Manager, Data Analyst, Store Manager, Regional Ops Manager, VP Store Operations
Source: workflow W1567 — Store Manager Self-Service Analytics Dashboard, Daily KPI Monitoring &amp; Actionable Insight Delivery</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1567_LaneSet3">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1567_Lane1" name="BI Analytics Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1567_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1567_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1567_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1567_Start4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1567_Lane2" name="Data Analyst">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1567_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1567_End9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1567_Start4" name="Daily — automated dashboard refresh at 6:00 AM (pre-store opening); real-time during…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1567_Flow12</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1567_Task5" name="Dashboard design">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Dashboard design: BI Analytics Manager designs the Store Manager dashboard with the following KPI modules: (a) Sales Today: (i) hourly sales vs. plan (bar chart), (ii) year-over-year comparison, (iii) top 10 selling items today, (iv) average transaction value vs. target; (b) Customer: (i) foot traffic estimate (POS transactions as proxy), (ii) loyalty penetration rate (% of transactions with loyalty card), (iii) BOPIS orders pending pickup, (iv) customer complaints today (from W41); (c) Inventory: (i) stockout count by department (SKUs with zero on-hand), (ii) overdue cycle counts, (iii) receiving schedule (expected deliveries today), (iv) inventory accuracy rate; (d) People: (i) staff attendance (actual vs. scheduled), (ii) overtime hours this week, (iii) training completion status; (e) Safety: (i) days since last incident, (ii) open corrective actions; (f) Peer Comparison: store&#x27;s sales per sqm rank within its region (anonymized peer benchmarking — &quot;You are #8 of 60 Mindanao stores this month&quot;)
Responsible (R): BI Analytics Manager / Data Analyst
Accountable (A): VP Store Operations
Duration: Initial design: 40 hours; quarterly refresh: 8 hours/quarter</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1567_Flow12</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1567_Flow12</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1567_Task6" name="Actionable insight engine">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Actionable insight engine: BI Analytics Manager implements automated insight annotations on the dashboard: (a) AI-generated commentary for notable KPI movements: (i) &quot;Paint sales down 15% vs. plan — foot traffic normal, conversion rate 8% below average. Check paint department staffing.&quot;, (ii) &quot;Stockout alert: 12 SKUs in lumber department at zero on-hand. Replenishment order expected tomorrow.&quot;, (iii) &quot;Loyalty penetration dropped below 40% for 3rd consecutive day. Remind cashiers to ask for loyalty card.&quot;; (b) threshold-based alerts: push notification to Store Manager&#x27;s phone when KPI exceeds threshold (e.g., sales &gt; 20% below plan at 2 PM); (c) weekly summary email (auto-generated every Sunday): store performance this week vs. plan, vs. last week, vs. same week last year, and key action items
Responsible (R): Data Analyst / BI Analytics Manager
Accountable (A): VP Store Operations
Duration: Setup: 20 hours; maintenance: 4 hours/month</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1567_Flow13</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1567_Flow13</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1567_Task7" name="Store Manager training &amp; adoption">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Store Manager training &amp; adoption: BI Analytics Manager ensures Store Manager adoption: (a) during new Store Manager onboarding per W1484: 1-hour dashboard training session; (b) during quarterly regional meetings: 30-minute dashboard best-practices sharing — highlight how top-performing Store Managers use dashboard insights to drive action; (c) track adoption metrics: (i) daily login rate (target: &gt; 90% of Store Managers log in before 9 AM), (ii) dashboard interaction rate (click-through from summary to detail), (iii) correlation between dashboard usage and store performance improvement
Responsible (R): BI Analytics Manager / Regional Ops Manager
Accountable (A): VP Store Operations
Duration: 4 hours/quarter</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1567_Flow14</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1567_Flow14</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1567_Task8" name="Continuous improvement">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Continuous improvement: Quarterly: BI Analytics Manager gathers Store Manager feedback: (a) survey: which KPIs are most useful? least useful? what&#x27;s missing?; (b) feature requests: Store Managers request additional views or drill-downs; (c) prioritize dashboard enhancements based on: (i) number of Store Managers requesting, (ii) potential operational impact, (iii) data availability; (d) release updated dashboard version quarterly with release notes
Responsible (R): BI Analytics Manager / Data Analyst
Accountable (A): VP Store Operations
Duration: 8 hours/quarter</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1567_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1567_End9" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1567_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1567_Annotation10">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-325 (ensure controlled execution — BI Platform &amp; Reporting (PA-28.1).) | - operational: standard operating procedures; system-enforced validation rules
Owner: BI Analytics Manager</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
